        "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061({x}^{3})}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x}.$",
        "worked_solution": "Applying the quotient rule, using the formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061x$ and applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061({x}^{3})}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x}) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061({x}^{3}))-\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061({x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x)}{{ln}^{2}\u2061x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-({x}^{3})^{2}}})\\cdot (3{x}^{2})-\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061({x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}}{{ln}^{2}\u2061x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061({x}^{3})}{x})}{{ln}^{2}\u2061x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061({x}^{3})}{x{ln}^{2}\u2061x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
